# followup-image-parity (finished by t1-image-parity, uncompiled: cargo was not run by the task)
# Lead: refresh Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack offline for resvg =0.45.1 (all its dependencies are in the
# cargo registry cache) and mixdog-js on mixdog-exthost-worker. The image-codec corpus (fixtures/image-codec) cases
# named "foreign avif ..." fail until an AVIF/HEIF decoder exists (none cached: needs dav1d or libavif or rav1d);
# every other case, including the SVG ones, is expected to pass. SVG pixel colours differ from librsvg by up to 2
# levels on blended alpha (tests/svg_reference.rs states it); sizes, acceptance, mime and alpha are exact.

Dependencies (crate-local manifests already changed):
- mixdog-exthost-worker -> mixdog-js (existing workspace dependency; no new external crate).
- mixdog-imaging -> resvg =0.45.1, default-features=false, features text/system-fonts/raster-images.
  This direct exact dependency avoids a hot workspace edit. resvg, usvg, tiny-skia and
  the codec/font dependency families have compatible versions in the existing cache.
  Complete offline resolution remains unverified because cargo was prohibited here.
  Lead must refresh Cargo.lock/workspace-hack offline; never fetch dependencies.

No CLI/compose/registry changes were made. Do not activate the native image routes yet:
- AVIF and HEIF still have no decoder. Existing AVIF fixture records Node success for
  probe/validate/resize even when called as PNG. ravif/rav1e in cache encode only;
  no cached dav1d/dav1d-sys/libavif/libaom decoder was found.
- SVG support now uses resvg; the original Node uses librsvg through sharp. The strict
  corpus plus svg_reference.rs must pass before calling that subset ready. Text,
  embedded images, gradients, filters and error sentences need broader parity evidence.
- No failure carve-outs remain for SVG/AVIF/WebP. The full corpus is expected to FAIL
  on AVIF until a decoder is supplied. A failure must not be waived as a removal.

Minimal safe integration proposal (lead decision, not applied here): keep all image.*
methods on the existing Node pool until native image decoding passes the strict corpus.
Do not use sniffed-content fallback or an environment toggle; current pool routing is
method-based. Keep native document methods independent. This is a temporary migration
blocker, not permission to retain product Node as the final implementation.

Known document parameter boundary:
- Actual read caller in mixdog-tools/src/fs/read.rs emits nonnegative integer
  maxOutputBytes. Whole JSON floating notation now preserves that limit too.
- Generic handler maxOutputBytes null/negative/fractional/string and noninteger
  maxPartBytes/maxContainerBytes remain different from JS arithmetic/Buffer.subarray.
  The extraction crate's usize/u64 limit API cannot express negative-relative slicing
  or preserve the original parameter spelling in the truncation suffix. This task did
  not silently claim those values are covered or add a new refusal. Full untyped
  parity needs a separate extraction-options change (mixdog-ooxml-text ownership).

Validation for the lead (not executed by this task):
1. cargo check -p mixdog-imaging -p mixdog-exthost-worker --offline
2. cargo nextest run -p mixdog-imaging --offline
3. cargo nextest run -p mixdog-exthost-worker --features test-support --offline
4. cargo clippy for both crates/all-targets with worker test-support, offline.
